      "claim": "The Context section's \"measured in this session\" claim that `git grep` reads a symlink's own blob for a match \"the same way\" it reads a regular file's, with a target string only \"rarely\" naming the subject, is false. Measured directly on git 2.47.3, git grep never searches a symlink blob's content at all, even when the target string is set to exactly the search term (0 matches, with or without --cached, -a, -I). This contradicts the prior spec SA-0372's own accurate note on the same behavior (\"a git grep over a tree lists no symlink, whatever its target string holds\"). It does not change what the cell must build, since the fix is correct regardless of the exact mechanism, but it is a false statement about current/measured behavior that should be corrected before a cell starts.",
      "criterion": null,
